  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943521/assets/0f920d90aa215300e720ace10bfec9292440d20f32c9b907854b984014f77427.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(Bx)+D,$ where $B$ and $D$ are constants. What is $B+D?$",
  "worked_solution": "The period $T$ of the function is\n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{6}-(-\\frac{\\pi }{6})=\\frac{\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nThe formula for the period $T$ of the function $y=A\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(Bx+C)+D$ is given by \n\n$$\nT=\\frac{\\pi }{B}.\n$$\n\nApplying the formula of the period, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\pi }{3}=\\frac{\\pi }{B}\\,\u27f9\\,B=\\frac{\\pi }{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}=3.\n$$\n\nThe parameter $D$ represents the vertical shift of the tangent function. We see that the function has been translated by $3$ units down. Hence, $D=-3.$\n\nTherefore, $B+D=3+(-3)=0.$\n\nFinally, the equation of the curve is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(3x)-3.\n$$",
